{
  "why": "What each CI arm COST THE RUNNER, keyed by the CI key its `##   ms | … | here=` line is printed under. `planCiShards` prices the shard partition off THIS and never off a standing row's `ms`, which is what it cost to ANSWER that row — for a CI-sourced row, a network call (trap 1068). `ms` is the MAX across the runs below, because a bin-packer fed the fastest sample packs a bin that does not fit; `minMs` is the MIN, and a shard is packed to the budget minus the widest `ms − minMs` among its arms (F2). Written by `node scripts/procgen/ci-gates.mjs --write-costs`.",
